---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout
  title="Drover Privacy Policy — Carson Underwood"
  description="Privacy policy for the Drover iOS app, an SSH client for herdr sessions on machines you own."
>
  <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-700/50 bg-slate-800 p-8 shadow-xl">
    <h1 class="mb-2 text-2xl font-bold text-slate-100">Drover — Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mb-8 font-mono text-xs text-slate-500">Last updated: August 14, 2026</p>

    <div class="space-y-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-300">
      <section>
        <p>
          Drover connects over SSH to <strong class="text-slate-100">machines you own</strong>.
          There is no service in the middle: no backend of mine, no account system, no
          analytics, and nothing of yours on anybody else&rsquo;s computer.
          <strong class="text-slate-100">I (the developer) never see your data</strong>, because
          none of it is ever sent to me. This app-specific policy supplements my
          <a href="/privacy-policy" class="text-cyan-400 hover:underline">general privacy policy</a>
          and takes precedence for Drover where they differ.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-2 text-base font-semibold text-slate-100">What the App Stores</h2>
        <ul class="mt-2 space-y-1">
          <li class="flex gap-2 text-slate-400">
            <span class="select-none text-cyan-500">&rsaquo;</span><span
              ><strong class="text-slate-300">Private keys and passwords</strong> — kept in the
              <strong class="text-slate-300">iOS keychain</strong> on your device. They are never
              written to a file or a log, and never transmitted anywhere except to the host you
              pointed them at.</span
            >
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-2 text-slate-400">
            <span class="select-none text-cyan-500">&rsaquo;</span><span
              ><strong class="text-slate-300">Host details</strong> — the name, address and
              username you enter for each machine, stored on the device only.</span
            >
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-2 text-slate-400">
            <span class="select-none text-cyan-500">&rsaquo;</span><span
              ><strong class="text-slate-300">Known host keys</strong> — the public key each host
              presented the first time you connected, so Drover can tell you if it ever changes.
              Public keys, held on the device.</span
            >
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-2 text-slate-400">
            <span class="select-none text-cyan-500">&rsaquo;</span><span
              ><strong class="text-slate-300">Local preferences</strong>, such as your terminal
              theme, font and type size.</span
            >
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-2 text-base font-semibold text-slate-100">What the App Reads</h2>
        <p>
          Whatever your own machines send back over the SSH connection you opened: terminal
          output, and the workspace, tab and pane structure of a
          <a href="https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr" class="text-cyan-400 hover:underline" rel="noopener"
            >herdr</a
          > session if you are running one. It is fetched to be drawn on screen. Drover keeps no
          history of it, builds no profile from it, and uploads none of it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-2 text-base font-semibold text-slate-100">Where Your Data Lives</h2>
        <p>
          On your device and on your own machines &mdash; nowhere else. Drover has no cloud
          component of any kind: no iCloud sync, no remote database, no crash reporting, no
          telemetry. If a host is not reachable from your device, Drover shows you nothing,
          because there is no copy anywhere else to fall back on.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-2 text-base font-semibold text-slate-100">Host Key Checking</h2>
        <p>
          Drover remembers the key a host presents the first time it sees it, and stops hard if
          that key ever changes &mdash; the standard defence against someone impersonating your
          machine. That comparison happens entirely on your device, against keys stored on your
          device. No key registry of mine exists to consult.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-2 text-base font-semibold text-slate-100">Third-Party Services</h2>
        <p>
          None. Drover integrates no analytics, advertising, attribution, or data-collection
          service. Its third-party code is
          <a
            href="https://github.com/apple/swift-nio-ssh"
            class="text-cyan-400 hover:underline"
            rel="noopener">SwiftNIO SSH</a
          >
          and
          <a
            href="https://github.com/migueldeicaza/SwiftTerm"
            class="text-cyan-400 hover:underline"
            rel="noopener">SwiftTerm</a
          >, both open source, both running entirely on your device, and neither contacting
          anything but the hosts you configured.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-2 text-base font-semibold text-slate-100">Deleting Your Data</h2>
        <p>
          Removing a host deletes its stored details and any credential kept for it. Deleting the
          app removes everything Drover has kept, since all of it lives in the app&rsquo;s own
          storage and the device keychain. Nothing survives elsewhere for you to request the
          deletion of &mdash; the data on your machines is, and always was, yours.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-2 text-base font-semibold text-slate-100">Children&rsquo;s Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Drover does not knowingly collect any information from anyone, including children under
          the age of 13.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-2 text-base font-semibold text-slate-100">Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
          If this policy changes in the future, the updated version will be posted at this URL
          with a revised &ldquo;last updated&rdquo; date.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-2 text-base font-semibold text-slate-100">Contact</h2>
        <p>
          If you have any questions about this privacy policy, you can reach me at
          <a href="/contact" class="text-cyan-400 hover:underline">cunderw.dev/contact</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
